axe_violations.fix:
1. Add Escape key handler to BottomSheet:
useEffect(() => {
  if (!open) return;
  const handler = (e: KeyboardEvent) => { if (e.key === 'Escape') onClose(); };
  document.addEventListener('keydown', handler);
  return () => document.removeEventListener('keydown', handler);
}, [open, onClose]);

2. Add role/aria to the sheet container:
<motion.div role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby={title ? 'sheet-title' : undefined}>

3. Add a focus trap using a sentinel + tabIndex management or install focus-trap-react.

4. Same fix for the route modal on /map.

Move the count announcement out of the icon area and into the Link's aria-label:
// In BottomNav tabs.map():
const label = tab.label + (hasBadge && tab.key === 'chat' ? `, ${chatCount} non lu${chatCount > 1 ? 's' : ''}` : '');
<Link aria-label={label} aria-current={active ? 'page' : undefined} ...>
  ...
</Link>
// Remove role='status' from DotBadge inner span; keep aria-hidden='true' on wrapper.

In createProfilePin() and createEventPin() and the cluster el creation in MapPage:
el.setAttribute('role', 'button');
el.setAttribute('tabindex', '0');
el.setAttribute('aria-label', `Profil: ${profileName}` /* or event title */);
el.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
  if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ') { e.preventDefault(); onClick(); }
});
Also wire MapCarousel (already rendered as accessible buttons) as the primary keyboard interface and surface a note in the PageHeader: 'Utilisez le carrousel ci-dessous pour naviguer au clavier'.

performance_issues.fix:
Dynamic import maplibre-gl:
const maplibregl = await import('maplibre-gl');
Move the import inside the useEffect that initializes the map (already guarded by `if (!mounted)`). This delays parse until after first paint. Alternatively use next/dynamic at the component level for the entire map canvas subtree.
